  "authority_effect": "none",
  "correspondence": [
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-1",
      "end_character": 291,
      "excerpt": "Authority is not truth, confidence, maturity, popularity, file ownership,\nrepository access, generated status, or implementation success. It may cite\nevidence and may be implemented by access controls, but neither evidence nor\naccess control becomes authority without the scoped owner route.",
      "unit_id": "unit-a778131bb3051c12878df8783b593198e7bbeae8583be2ba79e04e859089b3bb"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-2",
      "end_character": 204,
      "excerpt": "This target remains distinct from the sibling targets semantic.authority, semantic.responsibility reconstructed from CAV2-D34; shared source lineage does not merge their identities or validation purposes.",
      "unit_id": "unit-1802aec4473459bc802883489de7d808fff2deb0893ef9369bf9b86799e1db15"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-3",
      "end_character": 251,
      "excerpt": "Candidate Definition reconstructed from an accepted normalization scaffold and exact CyberAlchemy-v2 source sections. It is not admitted and grants no implementation, migration, registry, publication, release, deployment, or external-effect authority.",
      "unit_id": "unit-551051d584e8331e5ddcc495261d314ed89f7cf4cc2e9b5d89d0ceba64f24fbe"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-4",
      "end_character": 227,
      "excerpt": "Use authority whenever a source, file, owner, process, gate, validator, or\ngenerated view would make something count. Ask: count for what scope, by which\nowner, through which surface, with which operation, and with what effect?",
      "unit_id": "unit-2c1be3d3177e8f7a58751ff3a6121653c313be46fe2aad604640a27f79e666aa"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-5",
      "end_character": 22,
      "excerpt": "scope.shared-authority",
      "unit_id": "unit-d98b0dcc8c90b5d742e9beb805c5005c88770dc54b7c3939d5b7cc2388378d48"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-6",
      "end_character": 78,
      "excerpt": "Admission, activation, publication, release, deployment, and external effects.",
      "unit_id": "unit-8dec732fb5d927545d4bf5c1bea73405d34e388983cdba3240a36b63ba348803"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-7",
      "end_character": 88,
      "excerpt": "Meanings assigned to split or reclassified sibling targets unless explicitly referenced.",
      "unit_id": "unit-94bf2030418c421474ce1629a5f3255fde290758d03623f29467345f93ee9ea0"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-8",
      "end_character": 88,
      "excerpt": "Resolve semantic.authority-claim by its machine identity rather than its directory name.",
      "unit_id": "unit-14fba1a6ee91335a66426f09e6f6663d8d26ed69de814adfe7a9534ce1851ef0"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-9",
      "end_character": 84,
      "excerpt": "Challenge source drift through the L1 drift audit before relying on Authority Claim.",
      "unit_id": "unit-3ca47f7cfdf91c0d634f59f98bc7c50b2c098531350dbfc9bc0b63e25f1a19c6"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-10",
      "end_character": 633,
      "excerpt": "In CyberAlchemy-lab migration work, Authority Claim is a prototype meaning reconstructed from CAL-NORMALIZE-01. It remains non-authoritative until the correct Lab owner admits a fully validated candidate.\n\nSource context retained for reconstruction:\n\nIn CyberAlchemy v2, authority is the base term under existing local surfaces\nsuch as `CAV2-D3` authority layer, `CAV2-D13` authority promotion queue, and\n`CAV2-D23` authority lifecycle axis. It protects the stable repository from\nletting file proximity, generated indexes, ontology projections, inventory\ncards, source truth, or repeated usage silently become CyberAlchemy v2 canon.",
      "unit_id": "unit-6e9e319230e1e1aae743b05eccb0dad7e88a53559ec6ee378f2d3e79abd83f20"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-11",
      "end_character": 41,
      "excerpt": "/home/vrondelli/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab",
      "unit_id": "unit-ffa309e64b53ab85866dd9c0bce78b5cb2d9a40913e906c9ea92bc3faa5b2ed5"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-12",
      "end_character": 133,
      "excerpt": "It is a precise statement that someone has a particular right in a particular scope; making the statement does not prove it is valid.",
      "unit_id": "unit-7050194fa1360e0de76b5619e9bb9181ac05205e5afbebf2d509340817592236"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-13",
      "end_character": 291,
      "excerpt": "Authority is not truth, confidence, maturity, popularity, file ownership,\nrepository access, generated status, or implementation success. It may cite\nevidence and may be implemented by access controls, but neither evidence nor\naccess control becomes authority without the scoped owner route.",
      "unit_id": "unit-6005954949e0b94e7dbca1a83af2eedca6b72cb710c336849cd56f3530a6d13f"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-14",
      "end_character": 204,
      "excerpt": "This target remains distinct from the sibling targets semantic.authority, semantic.responsibility reconstructed from CAV2-D34; shared source lineage does not merge their identities or validation purposes.",
      "unit_id": "unit-979241f8f7ced5b8f3240cc10fee739adb5fc6a73a44d57f4c250386c800aeaa"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-15",
      "end_character": 376,
      "excerpt": "For an authority claim `A` over object `x`, CyberAlchemy v2 requires:\n\n```text\nA(x) = (scope, owner, surface, object, operation, basis, effect, challenge_route)\n```\n\nThe claim is admissible only if `scope`, `owner`, `surface`, `operation`, and\n`effect` are explicit. If any field is implicit, the authority claim becomes\ncandidate evidence or residue, not governing authority.",
      "unit_id": "unit-bcab6675c305c5f0f6ae64358c1cdecd6165658084fb3a9ff65bfb8a177e0f44"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-16",
      "end_character": 1161,
      "excerpt": "Authority Claim is the normalized definition identified by semantic.authority-claim, owned within scope.shared-authority, and carried by type.definition. Any canonical instance must preserve that classification and the accepted source relations to CAV2-D34 without silently merging it with another target.\n\nTarget-specific normative meaning:\n\nAn Authority Claim is an explicit, challengeable assertion that a named owner or owner route may perform a named operation over a named governed object within an exact scope, on a stated decision or evidence basis, with a declared effect.\n\nBound source-semantic basis:\n\nAuthority is the scoped right or responsibility to let a term, rule, status,\nartifact, relation, gate result, validation result, or mutation count for a\ndeclared CyberAlchemy v2 purpose.\n\nAn authority claim is valid only when it names the scope, owner or owner route,\nauthority surface, governed object, allowed operation, evidence or decision\nbasis, effect, and challenge or drift route. Authority may decide what counts\ninside its scope, but it does not automatically transfer across scopes,\nsurfaces, owners, generated mirrors, or source spaces.",
      "unit_id": "unit-89f2b95a8a4d9f492609df7c3d2185913cb81820311ad471b3423e4fe09615ec"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-17",
      "end_character": 47,
      "excerpt": "Stable normalized identity for Authority Claim.",
      "unit_id": "unit-7434fd4d795283d77df66fb18b2f6dbebbc1205fc55f0ffbc31fe11f214e6bee"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-18",
      "end_character": 24,
      "excerpt": "semantic.authority-claim",
      "unit_id": "unit-88a0020007900e757346b67026d8b51034e028ddc7d3209f057c6d359a9edb33"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-19",
      "end_character": 49,
      "excerpt": "Bound CyberAlchemy-v2 source-definition identity.",
      "unit_id": "unit-589257840cd95cd1a238672e86bd6b9137eba67d8ce5929322ef98c2127693fd"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-20",
      "end_character": 8,
      "excerpt": "CAV2-D34",
      "unit_id": "unit-7cbbc8a4dd7aea8948a69c28d11d53f5900522c8a84b2c46f2845d9d62fe7b70"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-21",
      "end_character": 62,
      "excerpt": "The candidate identity remains cal.definition.authority-claim.",
      "unit_id": "unit-9c3bc37e9fcdfe727f98bb38267eba9319c870ddac4d2063a630cf267d769ece"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-22",
      "end_character": 53,
      "excerpt": "Every selected source-section digest remains current.",
      "unit_id": "unit-62d9b9f0f2e14b44077e3a0db7904079fca058376b549a92223861c2220f97bc"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-23",
      "end_character": 51,
      "excerpt": "The machine record validates against Definition/v1.",
      "unit_id": "unit-6e0a36a3e7ce10e3274f2fe9e2ee41f7701f2c203d126d1278b94a5f3bd6b8fd"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-24",
      "end_character": 68,
      "excerpt": "The human projection is regenerated exactly from the machine record.",
      "unit_id": "unit-6e3477ec8786dca6eee728124933d1959d2501d9fa6c5a4a317baaec6d87d593"
    }
  ],
